---
import TopicClusterNav from '../components/TopicClusterNav.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy' }
];

const entityTags = [
  { label: 'Policy Type', value: 'Data Privacy & Transparency' },
  { label: 'Effective Date', value: 'January 2026' },
  { label: 'Last Updated', value: 'November 2026' },
  { label: 'Storage Standard', value: 'Client-Side LocalStorage' }
];

const quickStats = [
  { value: 'No Sign-Up', label: 'Personal Privacy', desc: 'Calculations execute locally in your browser with no profile created' },
  { value: 'Local Only', label: 'Saved Projects', desc: 'All dimensions and project estimates stay on your device' },
  { value: '100% Free', label: 'Open Access', desc: 'No registration, accounts, or mandatory logins required' }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Rock Coverage Calculator"
  metaDescription="Read our transparent privacy policy. Learn how Rock Coverage Calculator handles local browser storage, analytics, and data protection."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
  hideAds
>

  <Header />

  <main id="main-content">
    <PageHero
      title="Privacy Policy"
      highlightWord="Policy"
      badge="Transparency & User Rights"
      subtitle="At Rock Coverage Calculator, we believe calculations should be fast, private, and secure. We do not require accounts, harvest personal data, or sell user records."
      breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
      entityTags={entityTags}
      quickStats={quickStats}
    />

    <article class="guide-content">
      <div class="guide-container">

        <div class="aeo-quick-card">
          <div class="aeo-badge">Key Privacy Summary</div>
          <h2>Calculations, storage and sharing</h2>
          <p>
            Calculations run in your browser, and saved project zones use browser storage rather than a site account database. Loading the site still makes requests to hosting and third-party services. Sharing a project URL or contacting the site is a separate action that can disclose the information you choose to include.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Information needed to use the tools</h2>
<p>No account, payment details or personal profile is required to calculate a quantity. Measurements do not need to include your name, street address, customer records or private project documents.</p>
<p>If you email a question or correction, the email provider processes the message and the site receives the details you send. Include only information needed to explain the calculation; see the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Third-party advertising and hosting requests are described separately below.</p>
<h2>2. Browser Local Storage (Client-Side Storage)</h2>
        <p>
          To enhance your user experience, this website uses standard HTML5 <code>localStorage</code> technology. This allows your browser to remember:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Saved Project Zones (<code>rock_saved_projects</code>):</strong> Your active multi-zone project list, including dimensions, rock materials, and optional order parameters.</li>
          <li><strong>Saved Field Calibration Notes (<code>rock_coverage_field_reports</code>):</strong> Optional calculation and stockpile notes you choose to save locally in this browser.</li>
          <li><strong>Theme Preferences (<code>theme</code>):</strong> Whether you prefer dark mode or light mode.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Saved projects remain in this browser until you clear them or use a sharing or export feature. You can remove saved zones with “Clear All” or clear the site’s browser storage at any time. A shared project link can encode measurements in its URL; loading or sending that link exposes the URL to the host, recipient and services involved.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Fonts, Advertising Cookies &amp; Consent Controls</h2>
        <p>
          To render typography consistently across browsers, pages request font stylesheets and font files from <strong>Google Fonts</strong> (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>). We also use third-party advertising partners, including <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, to serve advertisements on eligible calculator and guide pages (utility, directory, contact, privacy, terms, and standalone embed views suppress ad scripts). These partners may collect and use technical request data and cookies (not including your name, address, email address, or telephone number) about your visits to this and other websites.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Third-Party Vendors & Google Cookies:</strong> Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites across the Internet.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising & DoubleClick Cookies:</strong> Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visit to Rock Coverage Calculator and/or other sites on the Internet. Read Google's official explanation at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Opting Out of Personalized Advertising:</strong> You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">Google Ads Settings</a>. Alternatively, you may opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">www.aboutads.info</a> or the Network Advertising Initiative opt-out page at <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">optout.networkadvertising.org</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Managing Browser Cookies &amp; Signals:</strong> You can disable or selectively clear third-party cookies in your browser settings, or enable recognized opt-out preference signals such as Global Privacy Control (GPC) where supported by ad partners. Disabling cookies can affect how some websites work.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Hosting Server Logs &amp; Technical Request Data</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not install third-party web-analytics tracking suites. Like virtually all standard web hosts, our hosting infrastructure may record basic technical request information when you load a web page. This includes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your internet protocol (IP) address</li>
          <li>Browser type, device classification, and operating system</li>
          <li>Referring URLs, pages visited, and timestamps</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These technical logs are used solely for diagnosing network performance, mitigating abuse or denial-of-service traffic, and maintaining reliable page delivery. They are not used to build personal marketing profiles.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Third-Party Services & External Links</h2>
        <p>
          Our guides and calculators may contain informational links to trusted technical standards organizations, such as ASTM International, AASHTO, state Departments of Transportation (DOT), and the National Stone, Sand & Gravel Association (NSSGA).
        </p>
        <p>
          We have no control over the privacy practices of external websites. When you click an outbound link to an external resource, we encourage you to review that third party's privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h2>6. European Economic Area (EEA), UK & Swiss Privacy (GDPR & Consent Framework)</h2>
        <p>
          For users residing within the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, or Switzerland:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the ePrivacy Directive, you have the right to grant or deny consent for the storage and accessing of cookies or other information on your device.
          </li>
          <li>
            Advertising and consent controls may be supplied by Google or other providers. Any consent interface shown when you visit describes the choices it offers; the presence of an advertising script alone does not establish consent or certification.
          </li>
          <li>
            Use any consent controls presented on the site and your browser’s cookie settings. Provider controls such as Google Ads Settings also govern options available through that service.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. California Consumer Privacy Rights (CCPA / CPRA)</h2>
        <p>
          Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), California residents have specific rights regarding their personal information:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right to Know & Access:</strong> You have the right to know what personal information is collected, used, shared, or sold.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> You have the right to request deletion of personal information collected from you.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Opt-Out of Sale or Sharing:</strong> We do not sell your personal identifying information for monetary consideration. However, under California law, sharing data with third-party advertising partners for cross-context behavioral advertising may be considered a "sale" or "share." You may exercise your right to opt out of personalized ad targeting using the <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gold">AboutAds.info</a> opt-out tools.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-Discrimination:</strong> We will not discriminate against you for exercising any of your CCPA/CPRA rights.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Children's Privacy (COPPA Compliance)</h2>
        <p>
          Rock Coverage Calculator is designed for commercial contractors, landscape architects, civil estimators, and adult property owners. We do not knowingly collect or solicit any personal information from children under the age of 13.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Contacting Us Regarding Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions, feedback, or concerns regarding our privacy practices or advertising disclosures, please contact our privacy and site maintenance desk:
        </p>
        <div class="contact-box">
          <p><strong>Rock Coverage Calculator</strong></p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:rockcoveragecalculator@gmail.com" class="text-gold">rockcoveragecalculator@gmail.com</a></p>
          <p>Website: <a href="https://rockcoveragecalculator.com" class="text-gold">rockcoveragecalculator.com</a></p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </article>
  <TopicClusterNav />
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-content {
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
  }

  .guide-container {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .aeo-quick-card {
    background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.3);
    border-left: 4px solid #10b981;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .aeo-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: #10b981;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .aeo-quick-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-bright);
  }

  .aeo-quick-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .guide-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .guide-content p, .guide-content li {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .guide-content ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .guide-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .contact-box {
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .contact-box p {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0;
  }

  .text-gold {
    color: var(--gold-400, #d97706);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
